# The one place a tool version is pinned. Nothing else declares one.
#
# Consumers, all of which read this file rather than restating it:
#
#   scripts/install-dependencies.sh   sources it, to provision a workstation
#   .github/runner-image/Dockerfile   takes them as build arguments
#   .github/workflows/runner-image.yml sources it to pass those arguments
#   .github/actions/versions          exports them into a workflow job
#
# They have to agree. A plan produced by one version of tofu and applied by
# another is the kind of difference nobody sees until it matters, and
# "works on my machine" is the whole failure mode a self-hosted runner
# invites. That was not hypothetical: CI validated pull requests on OpenTofu
# 1.10.6 for as long as this file said 1.12.6, because the workflow declared
# its own copy.
#
# tests/go/repo/versions_test.go asserts that no consumer restates a key.
#
# Its companion is approved-suppliers.yml beside this file: this one pins WHAT
# VERSION of a thing the estate takes, that one declares WHO it may be taken
# from. Two files rather than one only because this must stay KEY=VALUE for the
# shell consumers above to source it.
#
# Keys are alphabetical because dotenv-linter (which Super-Linter runs over
# anything ending in .env - see the note atop .github/super-linter.vars) fails
# the build on UnorderedKey. Grouping them by what they are for reads better
# and is not worth a red check; nothing here depends on the order.
#
# A checksum belongs beside the version it pins, because the two only ever
# change together. Node's are absent only because they are per-architecture
# and live in the one script that downloads it.
FLUX_VERSION=2.7.1
GO_VERSION=1.26.7
KUBECONFORM_VERSION=0.7.0
KUBECTL_VERSION=v1.34.11
NODE_VERSION=24.19.0
RCLONE_VERSION=1.75.0
RUNNER_VERSION=2.337.0
TALOSCTL_VERSION=v1.13.8
TOFU_VERSION=1.12.6
TRUFFLEHOG_SHA256=f863ea3a8d786f7d097870496c977944cce7372a2fe1e56707d965016e543ece
TRUFFLEHOG_VERSION=3.97.1
